.TH TX\-DECODE 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
tx\-decode \- one transaction on stdin (hex/base64 raw tx, PSBT, EVM RLP, or a JSON line with
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tx\-decode [\-\-chain btc|ltc|doge] [\-\-text] < transaction \-> JSON lines (or plain summary)
       tx\-decode \-\-nvc\-json TXID < api.novaco.in gettransaction JSON \-> raw tx hex (fails unless the hash is TXID)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
"psbt"/"tx"/"unsigned_tx"/"signed_tx") \-> public JSON lines, or \-\-text for a human summary.
Offline, no keys. Flags: \-\-chain btc|ltc|doge (address encoding for UTXO txs), \-\-text,
\-\-nvc\-json TXID (Novacoin explorer JSON on stdin \-> raw hex, hash\-checked against TXID).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
\-\-chain
\-\-nvc\-json
\-\-text
.fi
Each flag's meaning is in the SYNOPSIS usage line(s) above (taken from \-\-help).
.SH INPUT/OUTPUT
tx\-decode: one transaction on stdin (hex/base64 raw tx, PSBT, EVM RLP, or a JSON line with
"psbt"/"tx"/"unsigned_tx"/"signed_tx") \-> public JSON lines, or \-\-text for a human summary.
\-\-nvc\-json TXID (Novacoin explorer JSON on stdin \-> raw hex, hash\-checked against TXID).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Measured on Linux by the EXAMPLES below (scripts/gen\-man.py runs them):
.TP
0
no status field
.TP
2
last status bad_input
.PP
Not every tool uses the same code for bad input: some exit 1, others exit 2 (docs/FINDINGS.md D1\-14). Always read the last JSON status line. Status and failure codes: docs/REFUSALS.md.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ echo zz | tx\-decode
# exit 2, last status: bad_input
$ python3 "$R/scripts/e2e\-only/evm\-fixture.py" transfer | tx\-decode \-\-text
# exit 0, no status field
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, docs/getting\-started.md, recipes/README.md
